    "sourceHandles": [],
    "guide": "Uses the existing Process executor for installed Workflow-type Apps. Tool-type Apps belong in agent.toolIds; never change their type to bypass confirmation. processNodeId is the native local App ID, without the app: capability prefix. The App receives visible inputs; outputs remain private until their agreed keys are published. Team appRef requires immutable coordinates for an authorized published version; ask for missing coordinates. Do not substitute inline scripts for Apps. Read the recovery topic for compensation.\n\nDiscover the App contract before configuration: process receives scoped visible state, so its expected input keys must be available under the names its contract declares. Node edges do not rename fields. For tool-shaped calls inside an Agent, select a Tool App or MCP tool in toolIds instead. Publish only actual declared outputs through state.globalKeys. Read reference topic=configuration and topic=examples with node_types=[\"process\"] for a native example.",
    "summary": "Execute an installed Workflow-type App."
  },
